      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2016/10/eng@/~cl_8",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "in subsection (2), by inserting after the word “thereunder” the words “or a person who has been compounded under this Act and has paid the compound”; and"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2016/10/eng@/~cl_8__para_c",
      "@type": "akn:paragraph",
      "eli:number": "c",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2016/10/eng@/~cl_8",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "by deleting subsections (6) and (7). Substitution of section 37"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2016/10/eng@/~cl_9",
      "@type": "akn:clause",
      "eli:number": "9",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2016/10/eng@",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "The principal Act is amended by substituting for section 37 the following section: “Suspension or revocation of driving licence 37. (1) Upon the suspension or revocation of a driving licence under section 35 or upon the revocation of a probationary driving licence under section 35a, the Director General shall give the person concerned a notice in writing notifying that person of the suspension or revocation, as the case may be, and shall require that person to surrender the driving licence within twenty-one days from the date of service of such notice. (2) At the end of the period of suspension under subsection 35(1), a driving licence surrendered to the Director General under subsection (1) shall be returned to the holder and the points awarded against him, if any, shall be cancelled. (3) Notwithstanding this section, when a person’s driving licence is suspended or revoked under section 35 or 35a, the Director General may refuse or suspend any dealing or transaction applicable to that person under this Act.”. Amendment of section 52"
      }
    }
  ]
}
